# DNC Content Platform — conversion rules

Reference design: design/dnc-content-platform.html (static HTML/Tailwind prototype)
Design tokens: design/design-tokens.md

## When converting a screen from the prototype
- Find the matching `<section id="s-...">` block in the reference file and match its
  markup, classes, and spacing exactly. Don't redesign or "improve" the layout.
- Replace hardcoded example data (job rows, KPI numbers, etc.) with Django template
  variables / a queryset from the view. Never leave placeholder data in committed templates.
- The prototype fakes navigation by toggling `display` on sibling `<section>` elements
  via a JS `go()` function. Real pages use Django URLs and `{% extends %}` — do not
  port the section-toggling JS for page-level navigation. Small in-page toggles
  (dropdown menus, accordion sections, tabs within one page) can keep similar JS.
- Sidebar and header are shared across all screens — always use the partials in
  templates/partials/, never inline them per-page.
- Job/task statuses shown to users are only: QUEUED, RUNNING, COMPLETED, FAILED.
  Never surface Celery/Redis/infra terms in user-facing templates or copy.

## Styling
- Tailwind only, utility classes matching the prototype's patterns (rounded-card,
  shadow-soft, shadow-lift, text-ink/soft/mute/faint, etc. — see design-tokens.md).
- lucide icons via the same `data-lucide="..."` attribute pattern as the prototype.
- Don't introduce a second icon set or CSS framework.

## Django conventions
- Class-based views unless a function-based view is clearly simpler.
- Template inheritance: base.html → partials/_sidebar.html + _header.html → page template.
- Keep view logic out of templates beyond simple loops/conditionals.
